            "review_title": "Review at iSushi",
            "review_text": "Iliyan\nSofia, Bulgaria6 contributions\n1\nGood, could be better\nMay 2019 • Couples\n3.5\n\nWent to the dinner buffet. My advice would be - go as early as possible.\nAt 6pm your orders get processed with a decent pace, but once it gets packed, 30-40% of what you ordered will be missing and we also got wrong orders couple of times.\n\nThe language barrier is tough to overcome. At the reception there was a guy speaking really decent english, but all the waiters struggled with it.\n\nFood is tasty and if you come in early - well prepared. If the venue gets full , the quality of food sensibly drops - probably due to the amount of orders.\n\nHaving hidden charges almost dropped my rating to 2 stars. The menu prices don’t include 10% VAT, and you get charged for wet napkins. Really ISushi? Really???\n\nThe fares are a bit above average - draft beer - 60k, 1l sangria - 120k.\n\nIt was a decent experience, but a lot can be improved if they wish to have regulars.\nRead more\nWritten May 4, 2019",
